    {
      "field": "/features/2",
      "source_id": "readme",
      "quote": "`berth gateway`: one OpenAI-compatible port. Name a model and Berth starts its engine,",
      "method": "model",
      "model": "muse-spark-1.3",
      "checked_at": "2026-10-31T01:36:48+08:00"
    },
    {
      "field": "/capabilities/0/label",
      "source_id": "readme",
      "quote": "Chat models, image pipelines, voice engines, games and GPU apps\nlease the card instead of grabbing it",
      "method": "model",
      "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
      "checked_at": "2026-11-20T01:49:20+08:00"
    },
    {
      "field": "/capabilities/1/label",
      "source_id": "readme",
      "quote": "berth run --as llama -- llama-server -m model.gguf    # this engine now takes turns",
      "method": "model",
      "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
      "checked_at": "2026-11-20T01:49:20+08:00"
    },
    {
      "field": "/capabilities/2/label",
      "source_id": "readme",
      "quote": "berth status                                          # who holds the card, who waits, and why",
      "method": "model",
      "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
      "checked_at": "2026-11-20T01:49:20+08:00"
    },
    {
      "field": "/capabilities/3/label",
      "source_id": "readme",
      "quote": "queues the request by priority: `hold`, `foreground`, `interactive`, `batch`;",
      "method": "model",
      "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
      "checked_at": "2026-11-20T01:49:20+08:00"
    },
    {
      "field": "/capabilities/4/label",
      "source_id": "readme",
      "quote": "Berth reports any process holding VRAM without a lease, with its PID, name\n  and memory, and leaves it running.",
      "method": "model",
      "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
      "checked_at": "2026-11-20T01:49:20+08:00"
    },
    {
      "field": "/capabilities/5/label",
      "source_id": "readme",
      "quote": "`berth wire llama-swap` adds the lease to every model\nin your config in one pass.",
      "method": "model",
      "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
      "checked_at": "2026-11-20T01:49:20+08:00"
    },
    {
      "field": "/capabilities/6/label",
      "source_id": "readme",
      "quote": "puts a Docker or\n  Podman engine under its lease",
      "method": "model",
      "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
      "checked_at": "2026-11-20T01:49:20+08:00"
    },
    {
      "field": "/capabilities/7/label",
      "source_id": "readme",
      "quote": "moves its weights to system memory on a\n  drain and resumes from there instead of reloading from disk",
      "method": "model",
      "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
      "checked_at": "2026-11-20T01:49:20+08:00"
    },
    {
      "field": "/capabilities/8/label",
      "source_id": "readme",
      "quote": "`berth stop ENGINE` drains an engine on purpose,\n  `berth resume ENGINE` puts a parked one back, and `berth reclaim` stops what a stuck release",
      "method": "model",
      "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
      "checked_at": "2026-11-20T01:49:20+08:00"
    },
    {
      "field": "/capabilities/9/label",
      "source_id": "readme",
      "quote": "Berth drains your\n  AI engines until you quit.",
      "method": "model",
      "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
      "checked_at": "2026-11-20T01:49:20+08:00"
    },
    {
      "field": "/capabilities/10/label",
      "source_id": "readme",
      "quote": "Berth names what Blender, DaVinci Resolve, OBS,\n  Kdenlive, Premiere and After Effects hold",
      "method": "model",
      "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
      "checked_at": "2026-11-20T01:49:20+08:00"
    },
    {
      "field": "/capabilities/11/label",
      "source_id": "readme",
      "quote": "`[[claim]]` in `berth.toml` covers anything else",
      "method": "model",
      "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
      "checked_at": "2026-11-20T01:49:20+08:00"
    },
    {
      "field": "/capabilities/12/label",
      "source_id": "readme",
      "quote": "**`berth hold`** frees the card for a call or a game you start yourself.",
      "method": "model",
      "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
      "checked_at": "2026-11-20T01:49:20+08:00"
    },
    {
      "field": "/capabilities/13/label",
      "source_id": "readme",
      "quote": "**`berth gateway`**: one OpenAI-compatible port.",
      "method": "model",
      "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
      "checked_at": "2026-11-20T01:49:20+08:00"
    },
    {
      "field": "/capabilities/14/label",
      "source_id": "readme",
      "quote": "It proxies ComfyUI's workflow API too, so an image request queues behind the same lease.",
      "method": "model",
      "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
      "checked_at": "2026-11-20T01:49:20+08:00"
    },
    {
      "field": "/capabilities/15/label",
      "source_id": "readme",
      "quote": "a bookmark to a stopped engine's web UI shows who holds the\n  card and a Launch button",
      "method": "model",
      "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
      "checked_at": "2026-11-20T01:49:20+08:00"
    },
    {
      "field": "/capabilities/16/label",
      "source_id": "readme",
      "quote": "**`berth pull hf:org/repo:Q4_K_M`** downloads from Hugging Face",
      "method": "model",
      "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
      "checked_at": "2026-11-20T01:49:20+08:00"
    },
    {
      "field": "/capabilities/17/label",
      "source_id": "readme",
      "quote": "**`berth pull civitai:VERSION_ID`** does the same from CivitAI",
      "method": "model",
      "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
      "checked_at": "2026-11-20T01:49:20+08:00"
    },
    {
      "field": "/capabilities/18/label",
      "source_id": "readme",
      "quote": "**`berth models`** lists every model on the machine (GGUF, safetensors, the Hugging Face\n  cache, LM Studio and Ollama's stores)",
      "method": "model",
      "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
      "checked_at": "2026-11-20T01:49:20+08:00"
    },
    {
      "field": "/capabilities/19/label",
      "source_id": "readme",
      "quote": "**`berth verify`** re-checks pulled models offline and names any file that changed.",
      "method": "model",
      "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
      "checked_at": "2026-11-20T01:49:20+08:00"
    },
    {
      "field": "/capabilities/20/label",
      "source_id": "readme",
      "quote": "**`berth storage`** shows each model root's filesystem, free space against its floor",
      "method": "model",
      "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
      "checked_at": "2026-11-20T01:49:20+08:00"
    },
    {
      "field": "/capabilities/21/label",
      "source_id": "readme",
      "quote": "**`berth models export ollama`** turns a GGUF you already have into an Ollama model.",
      "method": "model",
      "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
      "checked_at": "2026-11-20T01:49:20+08:00"
    },
    {
      "field": "/capabilities/22/label",
      "source_id": "readme",
      "quote": "**`berth update`** asks the release page whether a newer berth exists",
      "method": "model",
      "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
      "checked_at": "2026-11-20T01:49:20+08:00"
    },
    {
      "field": "/capabilities/23/label",
      "source_id": "readme",
      "quote": "Berth reads llama.cpp, llama-swap, Ollama, vLLM, SGLang, ComfyUI,\n  Kokoro, LM Studio, KoboldCpp, TabbyAPI, LocalAI and more",
      "method": "model",
      "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
      "checked_at": "2026-11-20T01:49:20+08:00"
    },
    {
      "field": "/capabilities/24/label",
      "source_id": "readme",
      "quote": "Per-card memory, load, temperature, power and clocks; tokens per\n  second, queue, latency percentiles",
